---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import { defaults } from '../../../../lib/equipment/04-03/solver.mjs';
const base='/equipment/04-03/';
const manual='https://cns1.rc.fas.harvard.edu/facilities/docs/Oxford_Operation_Manual_220275_Part1.pdf';
const fis='https://media-moov-co.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/user_media/listingFile/77845/03da19656473458c975da1a0c773c4d9/4b5dd96633424aecbdfa517c7aef0fdd_oxfordplasmapro100cobra_f.pdf';
const ucsd='https://nanofab.ucsd.edu/facilities/';
const photo='https://nanofab.ucsd.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Cobra-300-768x564.png';
const fields=[
['waferMm','Wafer diameter (mm)',150,150,1],['substrateUm','Silicon thickness (µm)',10,1000,1],
['openingUm','Mask opening (µm)',2,200,.1],['maskUm','Initial mask (µm)',.05,20,.05],
['cycles','Bosch cycles',1,400,1],['stepUm','Zero-lag removal / cycle (µm)',.05,2,.05],
['scallopUm','Lateral scallop amplitude (µm)',0,.5,.01],['taperDeg','Inward taper from vertical (°)',-3,3,.1],
['selectivity','Si : mask removal ratio',1,500,1],['lag','Aspect-ratio lag coefficient',0,1,.01]
];
---
<Layout pageTitle="Deep silicon etcher" subtitle="" description="Interactive Oxford PlasmaPro 100 Cobra 300 Bosch deep silicon etch geometry laboratory.">
<article class="equipment cobra" id="cobra-lab">
<nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/04-03/">← Equipment 04-03</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#evidence">Evidence and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">04-03 · VIRTUAL MICROFABRICATION / DRIE</span><h2>Oxford PlasmaPro 100 Cobra 300</h2><p>UC San Diego six-inch silicon wafer / mechanical clamp / loadlock configuration. Simulated Bosch geometry, not an operating recipe or an instrument qualification.</p></header>
<div class="bench">
<section class="instrument"><h2>Instrument</h2><div class="toolbar"><button data-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-view="reference">Photo angle</button><button data-view="side">Side</button><button data-view="rear">Rear</button><button data-view="load">Loadlock</button><button id="cut">Inspect source / chuck</button></div>
<div id="view" aria-label="Interactive three-dimensional instrument" role="img"></div><p id="viewer-note" class="small" role="status">Loading scaled glTF asset…</p>
<div class="toolbar"><button id="lid">Open loadlock</button><button id="load" disabled>Remove wafer</button><button id="return-carrier" disabled>Return carrier</button></div><p class="readout" id="machine-status" aria-live="polite">Loadlock closed · wafer ready</p>
<p class="small">Internal source, coil, clamp, carrier transfer and pump placements are schematic. Opening travel is illustrative, not a measured service limit. The virtual interlock prevents opening the lid with the wafer in the chamber.</p></section>
<section class="settings"><h2>Sample and effective calibration</h2><form id="settings" onsubmit="return false">
<label>Sample ID<input name="sampleId" value={defaults.sampleId} maxlength="100" required/></label><label>Input revision<input type="number" name="revision" value={defaults.revision} min="0" max="1000000" step="1" required/></label>
<label>Mask material<select name="maskMaterial"><option value="photoresist">Photoresist</option><option value="SiO2">Silicon dioxide</option></select></label>
{fields.map(([key,label,min,max,step])=><label>{label}<input name={key} type="number" value={defaults[key]} min={min} max={max} step={step} required/></label>)}
</form><p class="small">These controls specify a synthetic effective calibration. Their ranges are software bounds, not equipment operating limits. No plasma power, gas flow, or actual timing is inferred.</p>
<div class="toolbar"><button id="run" class="primary">Transfer &amp; etch</button><button id="example">Run example</button></div><progress id="progress" value="0" max="1" aria-label="Virtual process progress"></progress><p id="process-message" role="status" aria-live="polite">Demo wafer ready; run the example or inspect the loadlock.</p></section>
</div>
<section class="outputs"><h2>Trench metrology</h2><div class="plots"><figure><svg id="profile" viewBox="0 0 360 240" role="img" aria-label="Trench cross-section"></svg><figcaption>Calculated cross-section, equal x/z scale. Gray = silicon; gold = mask; ivory = removed volume.</figcaption></figure><figure><svg id="wall-detail" viewBox="0 0 340 135" role="img" aria-label="Detrended wall scallops"></svg><figcaption>Detrended wall detail (last eight cycles), expanded lateral scale.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div id="result" aria-live="polite">No current result.</div><div class="toolbar"><button id="json" disabled>Export sample revision (JSON)</button><button id="csv" disabled>Export wall coordinates (CSV)</button><a href={base+'example.json'} download>Example output</a></div></section>
<section id="evidence"><h2>Configuration and illustrated reference sheet</h2><p>The UCSD tool is the selected installation. The dimensions below are from a different 200 mm Cobra family configuration and serve as provisional enclosure scale references only; they are not measurements of UCSD's six-inch tool. The serial number and installed pump variants remain unknown.</p>
<div class="reference-grid">
<figure><svg viewBox="0 0 280 200" role="img" aria-label="Original front elevation schematic"><rect x="38" y="71" width="99" height="112" rx="2" fill="#dddcd3" stroke="#565b5d"/><rect x="44" y="17" width="87" height="58" fill="#e4e3dc" stroke="#565b5d"/><rect x="45" y="37" width="85" height="12" fill="#233665"/><rect x="44" y="74" width="87" height="20" fill="#919a9d" stroke="#565b5d"/><rect x="46" y="94" width="84" height="22" fill="#d9d9d2" stroke="#565b5d"/><circle cx="113" cy="103" r="6" fill="#b82d23" stroke="#e3be37" stroke-width="3"/><rect x="185" y="86" width="70" height="97" fill="#dadad4" stroke="#565b5d"/><rect x="187" y="45" width="66" height="35" fill="#263e48" stroke="#565b5d"/><path d="M 220 80 v 6 M 12 17 v 166 M 8 17 h 8 M8 183 h8" stroke="currentColor" fill="none"/><text x="8" y="103" font-size="10" fill="currentColor" transform="rotate(-90 8 103)">1.738 m (reference)</text><text x="139" y="27" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">ICP</text><text x="139" y="89" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">Loadlock</text><text x="184" y="196" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">Control rack</text></svg><figcaption>Original labeled front elevation, inferred. <a href={photo} target="_blank" rel="noopener">UCSD installation photograph</a> (2025 image, Cobra 300): blue upper fascia, steel loading platform, E-stop and separate rack. <button data-view="reference">Compare model angle</button></figcaption></figure>
<figure><svg viewBox="0 0 280 200" role="img" aria-label="Original side elevation schematic"><rect x="28" y="94" width="135" height="89" fill="#dddcd3" stroke="#565b5d"/><rect x="94" y="17" width="69" height="77" fill="#e4e3dc" stroke="#565b5d"/><rect x="94" y="40" width="69" height="12" fill="#233665"/><rect x="163" y="76" width="70" height="16" fill="#929b9f" stroke="#565b5d"/><path d="M163 92 H233 V114 L207 127 H163 Z" fill="#dddcd3" stroke="#565b5d"/><rect x="32" y="108" width="52" height="54" fill="#cfcec7" stroke="#565b5d"/><path d="M28 193 H233 M28 189 v8 M233 189 v8" stroke="currentColor"/><text x="95" y="190" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">1.749 m ref.</text><text x="35" y="103" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">Service</text><text x="172" y="72" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">Lid</text></svg><figcaption>Original side elevation. <a href={fis+'#page=15'} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Oxford facilities interface, issue 01 (2022), printed p.13</a> supplies family envelope; see Fig. 2, printed p.5, for service panel and feet. <button data-view="side">Side view</button> <button data-view="rear">Rear view</button></figcaption></figure>
<figure><svg viewBox="0 0 280 200" role="img" aria-label="Original simplified process assembly diagram"><rect x="75" y="36" width="108" height="107" fill="#c8c9c3" stroke="#565b5d"/><rect x="111" y="42" width="40" height="80" fill="#e4e5df" stroke="#565b5d"/>{[0,1,2,3,4].map(i=><path d={'M102 '+(50+i*12)+' H160'} stroke="#a86c36" stroke-width="4"/>)}<ellipse cx="130" cy="135" rx="42" ry="8" fill="#5b6268"/><ellipse cx="130" cy="129" rx="29" ry="5" fill="#7ea5ba"/><path d="M183 127 H246 V143 H183" fill="#969ea2" stroke="#565b5d"/><path d="M185 123 L238 77" stroke="#565b5d" stroke-width="7"/><path d="M246 136 H266" stroke="currentColor"/><text x="5" y="55" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">ICP coil</text><path d="M48 52 H101" stroke="currentColor"/><text x="2" y="126" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">RF chuck</text><path d="M52 130 H88" stroke="currentColor"/><text x="183" y="67" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">Lid (open)</text><text x="174" y="160" font-size="10" fill="currentColor">Transfer</text></svg><figcaption>Original functional cutaway; internal scale, coil turns and pivots inferred. <a href={manual+'#page=62'} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Oxford operator manual, issue 1 (2016), printed pp.59–62</a> establishes semi-automatic carrier handling and separate source/bias. <button data-view="load">Loadlock close-up</button></figcaption></figure>
</div>
<p>Photographs and manufacturer drawings remain at their original sources; reuse permission was not established. Exterior silhouette comparisons are qualitative, not calibrated photogrammetry. The UCSD image establishes a three-quarter angle only; the side/rear views are family-informed reconstructions.</p>
<h3>Specifications and evidence</h3><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Specification</th><th>Value / conditions</th><th>Use / source</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Wafer and holder</td><td>6-inch class (150 mm nominal), clamp, helium backside cooling</td><td>Selected configuration; <a href={ucsd}>UCSD equipment</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>Substrate RF</td><td>13.56 MHz</td><td>Hardware identity; not solved, UCSD</td></tr>
<tr><td>Temperature capability</td><td>−150 to 400 °C</td><td>Hardware capability; not modeled, UCSD</td></tr>
<tr><td>Reported Bosch capability</td><td>&gt;8 µm/min; Si:PR &gt;120:1; Si:SiO₂ &gt;300:1</td><td>Recipe dependent facility claim; not fixture calibration, UCSD</td></tr>
<tr><td>Process-module reference L × W × H</td><td>1749 × 786 × 1728–1748 mm</td><td>200 mm family installation only; <a href={fis+'#page=15'}>FIS p.13</a>; nominal housing height 1738 mm</td></tr>
<tr><td>Rack / external pumps</td><td>Rack 639 × 612 × 1091–1102 mm; chamber pump 979 × 388 × 658–660 mm; loadlock pump 519 × 195 × 270 mm</td><td>Same family FIS p.13; placement and covers inferred</td></tr>
<tr><td>Loadlock lid and carrier transfer</td><td>Illustrative 79.2° rotation; 585 mm nominal horizontal displacement</td><td>Original design choices, not manufacturer travel; <a href={manual+'#page=49'}>manual p.48 interlocks</a></td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h3>Numerical contract</h3><p>Input is one masked 150 mm silicon wafer, one isolated straight trench opening and a user-supplied effective calibration. The model uses the recurrence Δd = d₀/(1 + k d/w), d ← d + Δd. At fraction u within each cycle, the wall half-width is w/2 − z tan(θ) + a sin²(πu). Mask loss equals total silicon depth divided by selectivity. Sixteen intervals resolve each scallop. A zero amplitude gives a smooth wall; this does not constitute a cryogenic etch model. Mask failure, through-wafer etching, invalid samples and intersecting walls are rejected before geometry is exported.</p>
<p>The <a href="https://plasma.oxinst.com/technologies/drie">Oxford DRIE technical overview</a> explains alternating removal/passivation. <a href="https://doi.org/10.3390/mi12050542">Gerlt et al. (2021), Fig. 1–2</a> shows physical scallops and aspect-ratio-dependent lag. The chosen functional forms are educational surrogates, not fits to those data. No RF plasma, heating, microloading, pattern interactions, mask lateral erosion or real process time are calculated.</p>
<p>Output schema <code>bts.drie.trench.v1</code> retains sample ID, parent revision, revision, input parameters, units and frame (+z into silicon), residual mask, resolved wall coordinates and cycle history. CSV is a numeric wall-only export; JSON is the complete sample revision. No compatible station import is asserted; the downloadable fixture defines the handoff.</p>
<h3 id="verification">Verification record</h3><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Executed result</th><th>Criterion</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Constant removal (20 × 0.5 µm)</td><td>10 µm</td><td>10 µm</td><td>Pass; 10⁻⁹ µm</td></tr><tr><td>Resolved local maxima after removing taper</td><td>20</td><td>20</td><td>Pass; exact</td></tr>
<tr><td>Mask (1 µm, 100:1)</td><td>0.9 µm</td><td>0.9 µm</td><td>Pass; 10⁻⁹ µm</td></tr>
<tr><td>Default and lag = 0.3</td><td>80 µm; lag lower</td><td>80; 56.39396 µm</td><td>Pass; direction</td></tr>
<tr><td>Mask reduced to 0.1 µm</td><td>Reject</td><td>Stopped before cycle 19 completed</td><td>Pass</td></tr>
<tr><td>Source geometry wafer diameter / housing top</td><td>0.150 m / 1.738 m reference</td><td>0.150 / 1.738 m by construction</td><td>Source scale check only</td></tr>
<tr><td>Independent experimental data</td><td>Measured process-specific wafer metrology</td><td>Not available</td><td>Not validated</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div><p>Numeric fixture was executed independently of the UI using the solver function. Repository tests reproduce it; test results from CI are tracked on GitHub. Rendered geometry is provisional.</p>
<div class="toolbar"><a href={base+'model-source.json'} download>Editable model source (JSON)</a><a href={base+'cobra.glb'} download>Download GLB</a><a href={base+'cobra.gltf'} download>Download glTF</a><a href={base+'output-schema.json'} download>Output schema (JSON)</a><a href="https://github.com/corbins-cryo-pod/buildthesimulation/blob/main/src/lib/equipment/04-03/solver.mjs">Solver source</a><a href="https://github.com/corbins-cryo-pod/buildthesimulation/blob/main/tests/equipment-04-03.mjs">Verification tests</a></div>
</section>
</article></Layout>
